     "type": "code",
     "head": "The trap: no base case",
     "say": "Now the bug everyone writes. Forget the base case, and every leaf calls walk on an empty child. That dereferences a null pointer. It's undefined behavior, and in practice a crash. So the first line of any tree function asks: is this node empty? That guard is the fix for the first problem, walk every node.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "label": "bug",
