     "type": "code",
     "head": "Trie: insert",
     "say": "Insert is the same walk, plus creating nodes. Each node has twenty six child slots, one per letter, and an end flag. Start at the root. For each letter, if the child slot is empty, create the node. Step into it. After the last letter, set the end flag. That's the green mark.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "struct Trie {\n    Trie* kid[26] = {};\n    bool end = false;\n    void insert(const string& w) {\n        Trie* u = this;\n        for (char ch : w) {\n            if (!u->kid[ch - 'a']) u->kid[ch - 'a'] = new Trie();\n            u = u->kid[ch - 'a'];\n        }\n        u->end = true;\n    }\n};"
      }
